gorithm (fairer but multiplies compute). I propose defaults-as-shipped with a small sensitivity check, but this is a choice you should endorse.\n- **Normalized score definition:** Uncertain whether you intend win rate (native, 0\u20131, well-defined for SMAX) or a return-based normalized score requiring random/expert reference points that may not be published for every SMAX map. This materially changes conclusions and needs your specification.\n- **Unverified repo claims:** Everything in section (2) \u2014 available maps, exact algorithm variants (IPPO vs MAPPO; QMIX vs DQN-style), logging metric names, eval episode counts \u2014 is unverified because no repository exists locally; I will rely on your setup topics to pin these down before finalizing the design.\n- **Threshold definition sensitivity:** choice of threshold (e.g., 50% vs 80% win rate) can flip which algorithm is \"faster\"; the design should report time-to-threshold at multiple thresholds or use fixed-budget curves (e.g., AUC of normalized score vs steps).\n\nNo experiment has been run and none is proposed to be run in this track. Please review this sketch; on approval I will produce the full experiment design with finalized controls, metric definitions, and analysis plan.", "evidence": "Verified via direct inspection: /workspace contains only task.json (410 bytes) holding the research question and a track.md note (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\"). Filesystem-wide searches (find / for *jaxmarl*/*smax*, depth 3) returned nothing; `python3 -c \"import jaxmarl\"` raises ImportError; pip list shows no jax/flax/optax packages. Environment metadata confirms no GPU, no network, no datasets. Therefore all JaxMARL/SMAX specifics (maps like 2s3z/5m_vs_6m, PPO vs QMIX/DQN variants, win-rate logging, steps/sec reporting) are stated from general knowledge of JaxMARL and flagged as requiring confirmation via the researcher's setup topics (setup_2, setup_4, setup_12) before the full des